TorchXRayVision DenseNet121 local research adapter

Architecture source: mlmed/torchxrayvision, commit
17726dd8f5e756eec3e5ae958281a289b05b1dae, torchxrayvision/models.py.
https://github.com/mlmed/torchxrayvision

Weights: torchxrayvision/densenet121-res224-all, revision
588eadcc6a744da71f8dce768bc974ec629443f5.
https://huggingface.co/torchxrayvision/densenet121-res224-all

The upstream library declares xrv.models, xrv.datasets and xrv.utils to be
Apache-2.0; the fixed weights' model card separately declares Apache-2.0.
The complete Apache License 2.0 is reproduced in LICENSE. Preserve the original
upstream license declaration and model card alongside distributed weights.

Local modifications: only the reviewed one-channel 18-output DenseNet121
architecture; removed torchvision, dataset loaders, downloaders, repository-code
execution, automatic resize, and operating-point output remapping. The model
loads only a fixed, hash-verified safetensors conversion. Conversion uses an
isolated, non-root, network-disabled container and inert source-class stubs with
an exact pickle-global allowlist. No legacy pickle is loaded by the runtime.
Output is the independent sigmoid of all 18 logits without diagnosis thresholds
or spatial localization. Synthetic conversion/inference checks establish no
clinical validation, DICOM preprocessing validity or population applicability.

The DenseNet implementation follows the torchvision architecture used upstream.
